<title>USA: US House panel propose federal timber sales target.</title>
<headline>US House panel propose federal timber sales target.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. House Interior Appropriations subcommitte Tuesday called for the Forest Service to sell at least 3.8 billion board feet of timber in fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>The proposed sales level was down from more than four billion board feet in the current fiscal year.</p>
<p>Over the last 10 years the level has been reduced steadily from 12 billion board feet, panel chairman Ralph Regula, an Ohio Republican, said.</p>
</text>
